---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config';
---

<SiteLayout title="Terms of Use" description="Terms for using Pilly and the optional Pilly Plus subscription.">
  <article class="legal shell">
    <header class="legal-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p>Effective {site.legalEffectiveDate}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="legal-summary">
      <strong>The important part</strong>
      <p>
        Pilly helps you record a routine you provide. It does not give medical advice, identify
        medicines, prescribe doses, or replace guidance from a qualified healthcare professional.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section>
      <h2>Using Pilly</h2>
      <p>
        You are responsible for entering accurate medicine names, schedules, instructions, and
        records and for reviewing them when your treatment changes. Use Pilly only in accordance with
        applicable laws and these terms. Do not attempt to disrupt the service, access another
        person’s information, or misuse account and storage features.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Not medical advice or an emergency service</h2>
      <p>
        Pilly is an organizational tool, not a healthcare provider, medical device, emergency
        service, interaction checker, or pill-identification service. Reminder delivery is not
        guaranteed and can be affected by device settings, permissions, battery state, software, and
        network conditions. Always follow the instructions of your prescriber or pharmacist. If you
        may be experiencing an emergency, contact local emergency services.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Accounts and private backup</h2>
      <p>
        The free tracker does not require an account. Optional Pilly Plus features require an account
        and an active entitlement. You are responsible for keeping access to your Apple or Google
        account secure. Backup begins only after you choose to enable it. You should keep any other
        records your healthcare needs independently of Pilly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Pilly Plus subscriptions</h2>
      <p>
        Pilly Plus may be offered as an auto-renewing monthly or annual subscription through Apple.
        The App Store shows the current localized price, trial eligibility, renewal period, and terms
        before purchase. Payment is charged to your Apple Account. Unless you cancel at least 24
        hours before the end of the current period, the subscription renews automatically. You can
        manage or cancel it in your Apple subscription settings. Trials, refunds, billing recovery,
        and family sharing are governed by Apple’s applicable rules.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Your content</h2>
      <p>
        You retain ownership of information and photos you add. You grant Pilly only the limited
        permission needed to store, process, synchronize, and return that content to provide the
        features you request. Do not upload content that you do not have the right to use.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
      <p>
        We work to keep Pilly reliable, but the app and optional cloud features are provided without a
        guarantee of uninterrupted or error-free operation. We may improve, change, suspend, or
        discontinue features. If a material change affects these terms, we will update the effective
        date and provide notice when appropriate.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Account termination</h2>
      <p>
        You can delete your cloud account from Pilly. We may restrict or terminate access when needed
        to protect users, comply with law, or address material misuse. Ending an account does not
        automatically cancel an App Store subscription; manage subscriptions through Apple.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Apple terms</h2>
      <p>
        Your use of the iOS app is also subject to Apple’s applicable App Store terms and the
        <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/">Apple Standard End User License Agreement</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms can be sent to
        <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
